  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Again, the very old bug popped up again. It's detection between Windows and Amdroid mode.\n\nWhen i make world for 1 hours or longer, and want upload it to Windows side, i get sometimes error, telling me my world is over 100MB and it's too big.\n\nBut that is Android mode setting. I am still in Windows mode, so why do i see sometimes this error message, it's annoying and i am forced to restart Unity.\n\nBut even i restarted Unity and after some minutes work on changes and upload again, it's still possible it will say world is too big. The chance is still there. I got 2 times in short time the 100MB size warning.\n\nHow is this old bug still there? Can you not make proper mode detection in SDK?\n\nI have reported long time ago same bug, and yet it's not even fixed.",
